<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Izyaslav of Polotsk</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1001">1001</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a> · Also known as Iziaslav Vladimirovich</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Izyaslav was a son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vladimir-the-great">Vladimir the Great</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyiv">Kiev</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rogneda-of-polotsk">Rogneda of Polotsk</a>, who was granted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polotsk">Polotsk</a>, his mother's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bantustan">homeland</a>, around 987. He founded the Polotsk branch of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rurik-dynasty">Rurikids</a>, which ruled the land separately from the rest of Rus' for centuries, and died in 1001, before his father. The chronicles remember him as a pious and learned prince.</p></div>
